pages = {
'our-story': ('Our story', '''<h1>Small projects. Real finishes.</h1><p>First Thread Studio is being built for adults who like the idea of making something by hand but do not want a second job disguised as a hobby.</p><p>Traditional needlepoint can begin with canvases, mesh sizes, thread conversions, finishing services, and instructions written for people who already know the vocabulary. We are designing a smaller first step: one original mini project, one core stitch, pre-sorted color, and calm help when the thread tangles or a row needs to come out.</p><p>The founding designs are original to First Thread Studio. Current product images are labeled digital visualizations while the production-format samples are tested. We will not open checkout until a true novice can complete the physical kit without live coaching, the thread quantities and print registration pass, and a real fulfillment date is available.</p><p>That is the whole idea: make the first finish feel possible—and make every promise earn its place on the box.</p>'''),
'how-it-works': ('How it works', '''<h1>Your first five stitches.</h1><h2>1. Open only what you need.</h2><p>Each planned kit keeps the canvas, color cards, tools, and first-step sequence together.</p><h2>2. Match the color.</h2><p>The printed canvas shows where each pre-sorted thread belongs. You do not need to choose a palette or translate a chart before starting.</p><h2>3. Learn one stitch.</h2><p>The core project uses a single diagonal tent stitch.</p><h2>4. Recover calmly.</h2><p>The planned quick-start and original video help show how to undo a stitch, restart a thread, and relax over-tight tension.</p><h2>5. Finish it yourself.</h2><p>The small format is intended for a patch, tag, ornament, coaster, or mini display without an expensive professional finishing service.</p><div class="notice">Final materials, dimensions, completion range, and finishing method will be confirmed from the approved physical sample.</div>'''),
'beginner-help': ('Beginner help', '''<h1>Start here when something feels wrong.</h1><h2>My thread will not go through the needle.</h2><p>Flatten and trim the thread end, place it through the included threader, then pull the threader—not the loose thread—through the eye.</p><h2>My stitches look uneven.</h2><p>Let the thread rest on the canvas instead of pulling it tight. The goal is consistent coverage, not maximum tension.</p><h2>I stitched the wrong color.</h2><p>Stop when you notice it. Use the blunt needle to lift the last stitch gently and reverse the same path. Do not cut through the canvas.</p><h2>The canvas is bending.</h2><p>Tension is probably too tight. Loosen the next rows. The approved sample test will determine whether optional support is needed.</p><h2>I need human help.</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:firstthread-studio@agentmail.to">firstthread-studio@agentmail.to</a> with the design name, a clear photo, and where you became stuck.</p>'''),
'faq': ('FAQ', '''<h1>The honest answers.</h1><h2>Is this really for someone who has never stitched?</h2><p>That is the design goal. The exact completion range and approved format will be published only after a true novice finishes the production sample without live coaching.</p><h2>Are the current product images photographs?</h2><p>No. They are original digital product visualizations and are labeled as such. Real sample photography will be added before checkout opens.</p><h2>Why is checkout closed?</h2><p>We will not accept payment until the physical sample, novice test, thread quantity, print alignment, landed cost, and fulfillment date are verified.</p><h2>Does the kit contain a needle?</h2><p>Yes. The planned kit contains a blunt tapestry needle and is positioned for adult use.</p><h2>How long will a kit take?</h2><p>No exact time has been published. The real range will come from the novice test.</p>'''),
'founding-drop-policy': ('Founding drop policy', '''<h1>Proof before payment.</h1><p>First Thread Studio will not accept a founding-drop payment until the product page states the approved materials and contents, shows a real production sample, gives the novice-tested completion range, and publishes a clear shipment date or window.</p><h2>If the founding drop uses preorders</h2><ol><li>The product page will clearly say <strong>Preorder</strong> before the add-to-cart button.</li><li>The expected shipment date or window will be shown before payment.</li><li>Customers may cancel for a full refund any time before fulfillment by contacting firstthread-studio@agentmail.to.</li><li>If the shipment date materially changes, affected customers will receive the new date and a simple cancel-for-refund option.</li><li>A preorder will never be represented as in-stock inventory.</li></ol><p>No deposit is currently collected.</p>'''),
'shipping-returns': ('Shipping & returns', '''<h1>Shipping & returns.</h1><div class="notice"><strong>Pre-launch draft:</strong> no processing-time promise is active while checkout is closed.</div><h2>Shipping area</h2><p>The founding drop is planned for delivery within the United States only. Carrier, service level, order cutoff, and delivery estimates will be published after fulfillment testing.</p><h2>Damaged, incomplete, or incorrect orders</h2><p>Email within 14 days of delivery with the order number and clear photos. We will replace the affected component or kit, or provide an appropriate refund, after verifying the issue.</p><h2>Unused returns</h2><p>The planned policy allows returns of unused, unstitched, complete kits in original packaging within 30 days of delivery. The customer is responsible for return shipping unless the order was incorrect or defective.</p><h2>Opened or started kits</h2><p>Started kits are not eligible for a preference-based return. Defects, missing materials, and quantity problems remain covered.</p>'''),
'contact': ('Contact', '''<h1>Ask before it becomes a problem.</h1><p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:firstthread-studio@agentmail.to">firstthread-studio@agentmail.to</a></p><p>Include the product or design name, order number if available, and a clear photo when the issue is visual.</p><p>No response-time guarantee is active during pre-launch. The live service standard and business mailing address will be posted before checkout opens.</p>''')
}
